		</div>

		<div id="main-content-area">
			
			
			<div class="container mainContent">
				<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">

<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@400;600&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --rouge: #DA002E;
    --rouge-dark: #B0002A;
    --noir: #1A171B;
    --gris: #6A6B6D;
    --gris-light: #F5F5F5;
    --gris-border: #E0E0E0;
    --white: #FFFFFF;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
  }
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: inherit; }
  body { margin: 0; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; background: var(--gris-light); color: var(--noir); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; }
  header { background: var(--rouge); color: var(--white); padding: 40px 40px 36px; text-align: center; }
  header .venue-tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: 0.75; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  header h1 { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: clamp(22px, 4vw, 32px); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 6px; line-height: 1.2; }
  header .subtitle { font-size: 15px; opacity: 0.95; margin: 0 0 4px; }
	header .address { font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.95; margin: 0; }
  .doc-wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 36px auto; padding: 0 20px 60px; }
  .section { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--gris-border); border-radius: 4px; padding: 32px 36px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .section { padding: 22px 18px; } header { padding: 28px 20px 24px; } }
  h2 { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--rouge); margin: 0 0 16px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gris-border); }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; text-align: justify; }
  p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 20px; }
  ul li { margin-bottom: 8px; text-align: justify; }
  ul li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  strong { font-weight: 600; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  table th { background: var(--rouge); color: var(--white); font-weight: 600; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: center; font-size: 13px; }
  table th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  table td { padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--gris-border); vertical-align: middle; }
  table td:first-child { font-weight: 600; }
  table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--gris-light); }
  .fee-table td:not(:first-child) { text-align: center; }
  .fee-table td.total { font-weight: 700; }
  .fee-table td.staffing { font-weight: 700; color: var(--noir); }
  .schedule-table td:last-child { color: var(--gris); font-size: 13.5px; }
  .schedule-table td:first-child { width: 180px; }
  .alert { background: #FFF5F7; border: 1px solid #FFCDD8; border-left: 4px solid var(--rouge); border-radius: 3px; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 14px; color: #7A0020; margin: 14px 0; }
  .role-block { margin: 10px 0; padding-left: 14px; border-left: 3px solid var(--gris-border); }
  .role-block + .role-block { margin-top: 14px; }
  footer { text-align: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--gris); padding: 24px 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--gris-border); max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="venue-tag">
  <h1>Performing Arts Venue — Theater</h1></div>
  <h1>Alliance Française de San Francisco</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Theater Rental Policy &amp; Fee Schedule</p>
  <p class="address">1345 Bush Street, San Francisco, CA 94109</p>
		</header>
		<div class="doc-wrap">
			<div class="section">
				<h2>1. Venue Overview</h2>
				<p>
					The Alliance Française de San Francisco (AFSF) performing arts venue seats 74 guests and is available for evening rentals by independent
					artists, nonprofit organizations, and private event organizers. All rentals are subject to the terms outlined in this policy.
				</p>
				<p>
					The venue is configured for seated events and is suitable for the following event types: presentations, conferences (with or without
					slideshow), and movie screenings. Concerts and theater productions may also be hosted at the venue; however, these require a separate
					agreement and are subject to additional terms and conditions. Please contact AFSF to discuss availability and applicable fees for these
					formats.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>2. Rental Schedule</h2>
				<p>The standard rental block is as follows:</p>
				<table class="schedule-table">
					<tr>
						<td>Setup</td>
						<td>5:00 pm – 6:00 pm (renter access begins at 5:00 pm)</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>Event</td>
						<td>6:00 pm – 9:00 pm</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>Venue Clearance</td>
						<td>Room must be fully vacated by 9:00 pm</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				<p>
					Any overrun beyond 9:00 pm will be billed at <strong>$150 per additional half hour</strong>. This rate reflects the continued presence of
					the event host, whose overtime compensation and payroll overhead apply for the full duration of any overrun.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>3. Fee Schedule</h2>
				<p>All fees are quoted per evening rental. Staffing is a separate fixed cost applied to all rentals.</p>
				<table class="fee-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Renter Type</th>
							<th>Base Evening Rate</th>
							<th>Catering &amp; Beverages (renter-provided)</th>
							<th>Staffing</th>
							<th>Total</th>
							<th>Total w/ Catering &amp; Beverages</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Independent Artists</td>
							<td>$700</td>
							<td>+ $150</td>
							<td class="staffing">$290</td>
							<td class="total">$990</td>
							<td class="total">$1,140</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Nonprofits</td>
							<td>$800</td>
							<td>+ $150</td>
							<td class="staffing">$290</td>
							<td class="total">$1,090</td>
							<td class="total">$1,240</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Private Events</td>
							<td>$1,250</td>
							<td>+ $200</td>
							<td class="staffing">$290</td>
							<td class="total">$1,540</td>
							<td class="total">$1,740</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>
					<strong>Catering &amp; Beverages surcharge (renter-provided):</strong> a flat surcharge applies when the renter plans to serve food and/or
					beverages on the premises, to cover additional cleaning and post-event reset.
				</p>
				<div class="alert">
					<strong>Alcohol Service:</strong> Under California law (Business and Professions Code §25680 et seq.), all persons serving alcohol at any
					event must hold a valid California Responsible Beverage Service (RBS) certification. This requirement applies to all renters without
					exception, including nonprofit organizations. Proof of valid RBS certification for each server must be submitted to AFSF prior to the event
					date. No alcohol may be served at the venue without prior verification of certification. Renters who do not have a certified server may
					engage the AFSF event host to serve alcohol for a flat additional fee of $125. Please note that the event host will act solely as the
					designated alcohol server and is not available to provide general catering or food service. This arrangement must be requested and confirmed
					at the time of booking.
				</div>
				<p>
					<strong>Nonprofits</strong> must provide proof of nonprofit status (IRS determination letter or equivalent documentation) at the time of
					booking to qualify for the nonprofit rate. Rentals booked without valid proof of status will be invoiced at the private event rate.
				</p>
				<p>A refundable security deposit of <strong>$300</strong> is required for all rentals, payable at the time of booking confirmation.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>4. Staffing</h2>
				<p>
					A mandatory staffing fee of $290 applies to all evening rentals. This fee covers the overtime compensation for two AFSF staff members
					required for every event, including a 22% payroll overhead to account for employer taxes, California UI/ETT/SDI, and workers' compensation.
				</p>
				<div class="role-block">
					<p>
						<strong>Front Desk Person:</strong> stationed at the building entrance to welcome and check in guests from 5:00 pm through 7:30 pm, after
						which the entrance is no longer staffed.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="role-block">
					<p>
						<strong>Event Host:</strong> an AFSF representative present throughout the event to oversee venue operations, ensure compliance with this
						policy, and remain on site until the building is fully secured. The event host is responsible for closing the building at 9:15 pm.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>5. Movie Screenings</h2>
				<p>Renters wishing to host a movie screening must comply with the following requirements:</p>
				<p>The film file must be provided in <strong>MP4 format.</strong></p>
				<p>
					The file must be submitted to AFSF staff <strong>at least 5 business days prior to the event</strong> date for technical testing and
					compatibility verification.
				</p>
				<p>AFSF reserves the right to decline screening of files that fail technical testing or that do not meet format requirements.</p>
				<p>The renter is solely responsible for securing all necessary public screening licenses and rights clearances prior to the event.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>6. General Conditions</h2>
				<p>
					Full payment of all applicable fees is due no later than <strong>10 days prior to the event date</strong>. Dates will not be held and the
					rental will not be considered confirmed until payment is received in full.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>All payments are non-refundable.</strong> Cancellations for any reason, including by the renter, will not give rise to any refund of
					fees paid.
				</p>
				<p>
					The security deposit will be returned within 10 business days following the event, provided no damage or policy violations are identified.
				</p>
				<p>AFSF staff reserve the right to end an event early if terms of this policy are not observed.</p>
				<p>
					Rentals must be confirmed in writing and a signed rental agreement returned to AFSF prior to the event date. The rental is not confirmed
					until full payment has been received.
				</p>
				<p>Renters are responsible for the conduct of their guests throughout the rental period.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="section">
				<h2>7. Daytime Rentals</h2>
				<p>
					The theater is also available for daytime rental on weekdays (Monday to Friday) and Saturdays, subject to AFSF operational schedules. No
					additional staffing fee applies to daytime rentals as AFSF staff are already on site during opening hours.
				</p>
				<p><strong>Daytime Availability (regular business days and hours)</strong></p>
				<table class="schedule-table">
					<tr>
						<td>Monday to Friday</td>
						<td>10:00 am – 5:00 pm</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>Saturday</td>
						<td>10:00 am – 2:00 pm</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				<p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Daytime Fee Schedule</strong></p>
				<p>
					Staffing is included at no additional charge during this . All other add-on fees and policies (catering surcharge, alcohol service, movie
					screening requirements, payment and cancellation terms) apply as set out in this policy.
				</p>
				<table class="fee-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Renter Type</th>
							<th>Daytime Base Rate</th>
							<th>Catering &amp; Beverages (renter-provided)</th>
							<th>Total w/ Catering &amp; Beverages</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Independent Artists</td>
							<td>$450</td>
							<td>+ $150</td>
							<td class="total">$600</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Nonprofits</td>
							<td>$550</td>
							<td>+ $150</td>
							<td class="total">$700</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Private Events</td>
							<td>$800</td>
							<td>+ $200</td>
							<td class="total">$1,000</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Saturday 1-5pm, Sunday 9-5 and holidays additional&nbsp;Fee Schedule</strong></p>
				<p>
					Front desk staffing is mandatory and charged at $60 per hour.<br />
					All other add-on fees and policies (catering surcharge, alcohol service, movie screening requirements, payment and cancellation terms)
					apply as set out in this policy.<br />
					<br />
					Alcohol service and AFSF event host are not available.&nbsp;
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="section" id="rental-request-form">
				<h2>Theater Rental Request</h2>
				<p>
					Complete the form below to request a rental of the AFSF theater at 1345 Bush Street, San Francisco, CA 94109. The AFSF team will review
					your request and confirm availability and next steps by email. Date requests are not a guarantee of availability.
				</p>
				<form id="theater_rental_request" methodajaxevent="_form_ajaxevent_0" onsubmit="triggerEventAjax(this, &quot;onsubmit&quot;, &quot;_form_ajaxevent_0&quot;, null, event); " action="https://www.afsf.com/about-afsf/space-rental/theater-rental/" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="theater_rental_request" value="submit" autocomplete="off" />
<input type="hidden" autocomplete="off" name="theater_rental_request_csrf_token" value="tFh7sk3EhmYVjD1E" />
<input type="text" name="_asname" value="" style="display: none" autocomplete="off" />
<input type="text" name="_asemail" value="" style="display: none" autocomplete="off" />
<input type="text" name="_asevtcount" value="" style="display: none" autocomplete="off" />
<input type="text" name="_astime" value="" style="display: none" autocomplete="off" />
<input type="text" name="_ashl" value="" style="display: none" autocomplete="off" />

					
					
					

					<h3>Organization &amp; Contact</h3>
					<div  class="formRow formRow1Col"><span class="formRowLabel">Organization or Individual Name</span><div class="formRowColWide">
						<input id="organization_name" aria-label="Organization or Individual Name" onchange="if (this.value &amp;&amp; this.value.trim) this.value = this.value.trim();" data-validations="\Controls\Forms\Validations\Mandatory" type="text" name="organization_name" style="width: 100%;" />
					</div><div class="formRowPadding"></div></div>
